<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Xtra-Vision takeover referred to Competition body.</title>
<headline>Xtra-Vision takeover referred to Competition body.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ireland's Minister for Enterprise and Employment Richard Bruton said on Wednesday that he had asked the Competition Authority to investigate the proposed acquisition of Ardnasillagh by Blockbuster Entertainment (Ireland) Limited.</p>
<p>Ardnasillagh trades as Xtra-Vision. Bruton said in a statement that he had asked the Competition Authority to report to him by January 31, 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;On receipt of its report, the minister will consider what further action, if any, is warranted by the exigencies of the common good,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
